  "details": "OpenSSL is a toolkit that implements the Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) and Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocols, as well as a full-strength general-purpose cryptography library.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation in CRL distribution point processing (CVE-2026-35189)\n  * openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via excessive QUIC packet buffer retention (CVE-2026-54873)\n  * openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via crafted CMP certificate revocation response (CVE-2026-75805)\n  * openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via inefficient QUIC stream reassembly (CVE-2026-42772)\n  * openssl: OpenSSL: Private key recovery via timing side-channel in generic elliptic curve operations (CVE-2026-54872)\n  * openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via unenforced QUIC connection flow control (CVE-2026-75804)\n  * openssl: openssl: information disclosure via non-constant-time SM2 scalar multiplication on ARM64 and RISC-V (CVE-2026-54875)\n  * openssl: openssl: Traffic amplification Denial of Service via QUIC packet over-accounting (CVE-2026-35191)\n  * openssl: OpenSSL: Private key recovery via SM2 timing side-channel (CVE-2026-77696)\n  * openssl: openssl: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds write during TLS context switch (CVE-2026-72897)\n  * openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via undersized DTLS record (CVE-2026-75806)\n  * openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via unbounded QUIC connection identifier backlog (CVE-2026-84784)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [AlmaLinux 10.3]OpenSSL silently uses default provider when `fips.so` is missing on systems in FIPS mode (JIRA:RHEL-213740)\n  * OpenSSL fails to initialize when automatic initialization happens in threads (JIRA:RHEL-252344)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
